{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04AS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-limits-exist}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2c51efac6cbb691d7cdbe11f357625c9fc6c3e8de5f6bbae3a6c54be8728c86b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f8a9db6461940297957993a799124205e0ebd947ae96f42ed963bc22abe3ba64", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Finite limits exist in <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Finite products and equalizers exist.\n<STRUCT_0004> The category has a final object and fibre products exist.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d6d1eb78d4743874b3a42fd43f8ee6db13083045ad851969d4b71d385107f398", "unit_id": "tag:002O:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04AS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\times B$", "MATH_0002": "$a, b : A \\to B$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$a, b$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n(A \\times_{a, B, b} A)\\times_{(\\text{pr}_1, \\text{pr}_2), A \\times A, \\Delta} A.\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-limits-products-equalizers}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6e43e24e3d9195793e87aa03b653988e5cb9800cf7844ef124e2c92e2ca62a59", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b58251763b1cc9eb017468939687a729a6485350d4401a43e2cbfbe38e97c287", "source_text": "Since finite products, fibre products, equalizers, and final objects\nare limits over finite index categories we see that (1) implies both (2)\nand (3). By\nLemma <REF_0001>\nabove we see that (2) implies (1). Assume (3).\nNote that the product <MATH_0001> is the fibre product over the\nfinal object. If <MATH_0002> are morphisms of <MATH_0003>, then the\nequalizer of <MATH_0004> is\n<MATH_0005>\nThus (3) implies (2) and the lemma is proved.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f0df2e9f06303539e073eab9b2dd235e9eb2b1bd21398a3f11ee335711f9312", "unit_id": "tag:002O:proof"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04AS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-colimits-exist}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c0f0df21fd5bf03ac80850077883ce0cc992127aed19159a6abeeb0df016bd72", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:879d4b64880ac23c67be6564af5d64a161ad41cc72e1a0fc567d62c86b866bc4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Finite colimits exist in <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Finite coproducts and coequalizers exist in <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0004> The category has an initial object and pushouts exist.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:efc4cdb959568cb08b483df3c5f9b6b2497f78b3abab93906a16da75bc2dbbda", "unit_id": "tag:002Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04AS", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-limits-exist}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4452ccd1a55e32405aeee7f91fd8903176598b1b73048454eb7a1606da35ddf8", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: This is dual to Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5df9307161914b8b28949be171f4da52bcf24ddaf81c69caf3cca8f6a3062c82", "unit_id": "tag:002Q:proof"}
